WEBVTT

00:01.160 --> 00:03.160
!!! REMEMBER TO ADD EDGEBLUR TO THE SUB TEXT, >>>>>>>>>NOT<<<<<<<<< THE LOGO/TS/OP/ED

00:03.690 --> 00:07.520
Episode 12 :

00:03.690 --> 00:07.520
" Cats on a Roof "

00:14.240 --> 00:16.450
It's time to go shopping, Yune.

00:16.450 --> 00:17.990
Go get ready.

00:17.990 --> 00:18.910
Okay.

00:18.910 --> 00:21.950
Grandpa, is there anything in particular we need to buy?

00:21.950 --> 00:23.920
Let's see...

00:23.920 --> 00:28.000
I feel like having some of Yune's sukiyaki again.

00:28.500 --> 00:30.250
Really?!

00:34.260 --> 00:36.180
It's good to have once in a while.

00:36.970 --> 00:37.930
Indeed!

00:42.850 --> 00:44.980
Hey, Claude, Yune-chan.

00:44.980 --> 00:46.440
Hello.

00:46.440 --> 00:47.690
Hello.

00:47.690 --> 00:49.610
The weather is very nice today.

00:49.610 --> 00:51.730
It's probably thanks to you.

01:06.210 --> 01:07.330
You're too slow!

01:07.330 --> 01:08.170
I'll leave you behind!

01:08.170 --> 01:09.340
Wait!

01:09.340 --> 01:11.210
That's quite the order.

01:11.210 --> 01:12.920
We're gonna sell it all!

01:13.590 --> 01:15.470
That's your husband's fault!

01:15.470 --> 01:16.680
Right?

01:16.680 --> 01:17.760
Claude?

01:18.390 --> 01:23.100
Where's the little black cat that's been clinging to your back lately?

01:23.100 --> 01:23.930
Huh?

01:25.600 --> 01:26.810
Yune...!

01:30.520 --> 01:32.400
Are there cats in Japan?

01:32.400 --> 01:32.940
Yes.

01:32.940 --> 01:35.490
The cats in Nagasaki have round tails.

01:35.490 --> 01:36.820
Oh.

01:40.870 --> 01:43.370
Looks like it likes you.

01:43.370 --> 01:44.410
Yannick-san.

01:44.410 --> 01:45.750
Hey.

01:45.750 --> 01:47.000
Claude-sama.

01:47.330 --> 01:51.380
<i>Japonaise</i>, your French has improved a lot.

01:47.330 --> 01:51.380
For those of you who forgot, <i>Japonaise</i> means "Japanese girl" in French.

01:51.880 --> 01:53.630
Thank you!

01:53.630 --> 01:57.130
Don't teach her weird things, all right?

01:57.930 --> 02:03.390
They told me that your Father made this store's sign.

02:06.140 --> 02:08.060
What's there to be upset about?

02:08.310 --> 02:12.440
The reason I've stayed here is because of this sign.

02:14.150 --> 02:16.110
Don't get too absorbed into the cat.

02:16.110 --> 02:20.160
Is this cat the one on the sign?

02:20.160 --> 02:22.120
No, that's a different one.

02:22.370 --> 02:26.080
The one on the sign appears infrequently, and doesn't come back for a long time.

02:26.080 --> 02:29.580
It has a big bell on its neck, just like the one on the sign.

02:33.090 --> 02:37.090
Could you tell it to come back if you see it?

02:37.670 --> 02:38.630
Yes!

02:45.180 --> 02:47.890
We're back, Oscar-sama.

02:48.480 --> 02:49.890
Welcome back.

02:50.730 --> 02:52.730
Oh, that smells nice.

02:56.070 --> 02:57.820
Shall we eat it now?

02:57.820 --> 02:58.530
Yes!

02:58.530 --> 02:59.650
I'll pass.

02:59.650 --> 03:00.530
I have work to do.

03:18.670 --> 03:23.390
<i>You said you didn't need to know more about Yune not because you trusted her,</i>

03:23.390 --> 03:26.060
<i>but because you were afraid to know, right?</i>

03:26.060 --> 03:27.060
<i>Afraid?</i>

03:27.060 --> 03:28.020
<i>Why would I be?</i>

03:28.850 --> 03:34.770
<i>The more you know, the harder
it'll be when Yune leaves.</i>

03:38.110 --> 03:41.360
Is there anything I can help with?

03:41.360 --> 03:42.490
It's fine;

03:42.490 --> 03:45.490
the metal's hot, so you'd burn yourself.

03:45.490 --> 03:48.160
Your thin arms definitely wouldn't be of any help anyway.

03:48.160 --> 03:50.910
I'm pretty strong!

03:52.790 --> 03:54.920
Hey, don't overdo it!

03:54.920 --> 03:55.880
Grandpa!

03:55.880 --> 03:57.290
Don't just watch her! Stop her!

03:57.290 --> 04:01.220
This reminds me of when you were younger.

04:01.220 --> 04:03.180
When Claude-sama was little?!

04:05.640 --> 04:08.640
Sure, there was a time when I was younger.

04:08.640 --> 04:11.680
You always tried to help your dad, and-

04:11.680 --> 04:12.770
Don't say anything more.

04:30.330 --> 04:31.250
Hey...

04:31.250 --> 04:33.620
Can I borrow these?

04:33.620 --> 04:36.080
I wouldn't burn myself if I have...

04:39.840 --> 04:41.840
Just go away already!

04:53.850 --> 04:55.980
Go... outside.

04:55.980 --> 04:57.310
I'm sorry.

05:18.380 --> 05:21.170
Why don't you just tell Yune?

05:21.170 --> 05:24.590
Think about how Yune feels to get scolded for seemingly no reason.

05:26.510 --> 05:30.050
No matter how much I tell her about myself,

05:30.050 --> 05:31.890
Yune won't change a bit.

05:31.890 --> 05:34.480
It isn't anything important anyway,

05:34.480 --> 05:39.190
and telling her would just make her worry more.

05:39.190 --> 05:40.810
I don't need to tell her.

05:41.770 --> 05:42.940
If you say so.

05:47.150 --> 05:47.910
Grandpa!

05:54.540 --> 05:56.290
Oscar-sama...

05:56.290 --> 05:57.790
I, uh...

05:57.790 --> 05:59.210
Don't worry about it.

05:59.210 --> 06:01.090
You didn't do anything bad.

06:01.340 --> 06:02.550
But...

06:07.010 --> 06:12.970
You chose those gloves because they were the smallest on the rack, right?

06:13.510 --> 06:14.430
Yes.

06:14.770 --> 06:17.390
Those were a memento of Jean...

06:17.390 --> 06:20.020
Claude's father.

06:22.610 --> 06:25.360
Jean was a small man.

06:25.610 --> 06:29.450
He was skilled at making intricate
designs with his small hands.

06:31.620 --> 06:33.830
Um... I...

06:34.870 --> 06:36.120
Don't worry.

06:36.120 --> 06:39.420
He isn't treasuring them in any way.

06:40.040 --> 06:44.630
They've just been hanging there, untouched.

06:46.880 --> 06:48.170
Oh yeah, Yune.

06:48.170 --> 06:51.180
I have a message from Claude.

06:52.470 --> 06:54.510
"I told you to go somewhere,

06:54.510 --> 06:58.520
but stay in the <i>Galerie</i>."

07:02.690 --> 07:03.690
Okay.

07:23.790 --> 07:26.250
Yannick-san's cat...

08:37.070 --> 08:38.660
Grandpa, where's Yune?

08:38.660 --> 08:40.200
She isn't here?

08:40.200 --> 08:42.330
Maybe she went on a walk.

08:42.330 --> 08:45.540
Did you tell her to stay in the <i>Galerie</i>?

08:45.540 --> 08:46.580
Yeah.

08:49.500 --> 08:51.960
Want me to keep an eye on the fire?

08:51.960 --> 08:52.970
Yeah, thanks.

08:59.470 --> 09:02.850
She'd better be in the <i>Galerie</i>...

09:02.850 --> 09:05.140
She <i>always</i> does this!

09:06.940 --> 09:08.810
Did Yune come this way?

09:08.810 --> 09:11.650
No, we would've noticed if she did.

09:11.650 --> 09:12.360
Thanks.

09:14.240 --> 09:15.820
Is she lost again?

09:15.820 --> 09:17.700
Hm, then on my next day off-

09:17.700 --> 09:18.530
Alan!

09:20.530 --> 09:22.490
Have you seen Yune around?

09:22.490 --> 09:24.000
What's wrong?

09:24.000 --> 09:26.040
I can't seem to find her.

09:26.960 --> 09:29.290
Did you scold Yune again?

09:29.290 --> 09:31.040
What the hell are you saying?

09:31.040 --> 09:33.960
Maybe she went outside the <i>Galerie</i>.

09:41.720 --> 09:42.810
No way...

09:44.930 --> 09:48.060
Put a bell on her if you're that worried!

09:50.610 --> 09:51.820
What's wrong?

10:09.290 --> 10:11.420
What's wrong, Claude?

10:11.960 --> 10:14.090
Those are Alice's...

10:14.670 --> 10:15.840
Excuse us.

10:15.840 --> 10:16.630
Alice!

10:17.880 --> 10:19.090
Claude?

10:19.090 --> 10:20.010
Where's Yune?

10:21.140 --> 10:25.640
Claude, you don't know where Yune-chan is?

10:25.640 --> 10:27.890
Claude, did you manage to find Yune?

10:28.850 --> 10:30.770
What is the meaning of this?

10:31.150 --> 10:33.150
Yune-chan ran away?!

10:33.150 --> 10:35.820
No, it's not something that serious.

10:35.820 --> 10:36.940
She probably went on a walk...

10:36.940 --> 10:40.110
So she hasn't come back from a walk yet, huh?

10:40.110 --> 10:43.580
Claude! What did you do to Yune-chan?!

10:43.580 --> 10:45.040
Nothing really...

10:45.490 --> 10:48.040
I did tell her to go outside,

10:48.040 --> 10:49.410
but I didn't kick her out.

10:49.410 --> 10:54.550
You're such a blockhead! You keep hurting Yune-chan!

10:55.300 --> 10:59.800
Anyway, finding Yune-chan is our first priority.

10:59.800 --> 11:01.050
Any ideas?

11:03.390 --> 11:04.640
Maybe...

11:04.640 --> 11:06.060
Yannick-san's...

11:06.060 --> 11:09.060
Then hurry up and go there!

11:09.060 --> 11:12.480
Geez, you're so useless, Claude Claudel.

11:12.480 --> 11:17.650
Edgar! You three are to look for Yune in every single nook and cranny.

11:17.650 --> 11:18.360
Yes, ma'am.

11:18.360 --> 11:19.820
Leave it to us.

11:20.570 --> 11:25.490
If she actually ran away, then I'm definitely taking Yune-chan under my care after this.

11:51.560 --> 11:54.310
Onee-sama, have you seen Yune-chan?!

11:54.610 --> 11:57.770
I haven't. What's wrong, Alice-chan?

11:57.770 --> 12:00.030
Yune-chan's missing!

12:00.030 --> 12:03.240
This is exactly why I can't trust Claude!

12:03.240 --> 12:07.410
Onee-sama, tell me immediately
if you find Yune looking for me!

12:09.080 --> 12:12.460
She gets so excited when it comes to Yune-chan.

12:13.250 --> 12:17.710
I can take it from here, so please go help Alice-chan.

12:17.710 --> 12:18.300
Yes, ma'am.

12:18.670 --> 12:23.130
Have you seen a Japanese girl about this tall?

12:23.130 --> 12:24.380
I'm not sure...

12:27.220 --> 12:28.720
Yune-sama?

12:28.720 --> 12:30.140
Yune-sama!

12:30.140 --> 12:32.140
I see, thank you.

12:32.140 --> 12:33.690
How is it going over here?

12:34.730 --> 12:36.060
Yune?

12:36.060 --> 12:37.440
Yune-chan!

12:40.650 --> 12:42.740
Where are you?

12:44.910 --> 12:48.450
Yune-chan!!!

12:51.160 --> 12:52.330
Yannick-san!

12:52.910 --> 12:54.750
Is Yune here?

12:54.750 --> 12:57.130
She passed by a bit ago.

12:58.170 --> 13:01.000
She was looking at my sign.

13:01.550 --> 13:02.670
Your sign?

13:19.360 --> 13:20.570
Yune!

13:24.990 --> 13:27.780
Don't look down...

13:44.720 --> 13:46.090
That idiot!

13:46.300 --> 13:48.340
I told her to stay <i>in</i> the <i>Galerie</i>,

13:48.340 --> 13:50.010
not <i>on</i> it!

13:52.720 --> 13:53.930
Yune!

13:54.310 --> 13:55.770
Claude-sama...

13:55.770 --> 13:57.270
What the hell are you doing?

13:57.270 --> 13:58.520
Come back now!

13:59.190 --> 14:01.650
I heard a bell jingling!

14:01.940 --> 14:03.110
A bell?!

14:03.110 --> 14:06.240
It must be the cat on that sign!

14:06.240 --> 14:09.240
I want to bring it to see Yannick-san!

14:09.780 --> 14:12.490
Are you taking that guy's story seriously?!

14:12.990 --> 14:15.200
Listen, that was just a joke!

14:15.200 --> 14:18.500
That cat's been missing for ten years!

14:18.830 --> 14:20.000
But...

14:20.000 --> 14:22.210
Fine! Just stay put!

14:23.880 --> 14:27.840
The moment Yannick-san put the bell on the cat's collar,

14:27.840 --> 14:30.760
it ran off because it hated the bell.

14:30.760 --> 14:33.760
It's been missing for over ten years ever since.

14:33.760 --> 14:34.850
No...

14:35.350 --> 14:37.770
Ironic, isn't it?

14:37.770 --> 14:42.060
He put the bell on it to make sure it was always nearby.

14:42.650 --> 14:44.070
I'm sorry.

14:44.070 --> 14:47.900
I thought I could help the <i>Galerie</i>...

14:47.900 --> 14:52.120
You're under enough stress being in a new place, right?

14:52.120 --> 14:54.990
Why do you always get involved in more trouble?

14:57.200 --> 15:03.170
The most troubling thing for me is to be the only one who can't do anything.

15:06.920 --> 15:10.880
Your job is to stay safe and by my side!

15:12.720 --> 15:16.850
I can't do anything else...?

15:16.850 --> 15:17.680
Don't move!

15:26.940 --> 15:29.190
I'm sorry, I'm fine.

15:29.190 --> 15:31.030
Hurry up!

15:31.570 --> 15:33.450
Hurry up and take my hand!

15:38.660 --> 15:42.000
That glass could break at any second!

15:46.670 --> 15:49.510
You don't know...

15:49.880 --> 15:53.930
the despair I had when I couldn't
grab anything with this hand...

15:53.930 --> 15:58.520
You aren't the only one who can't do anything!

15:59.270 --> 16:02.270
Both Grandpa and I are the same!

16:29.250 --> 16:31.300
Don't do this again, all right?

16:31.300 --> 16:32.760
I'm sorry.

16:32.760 --> 16:35.760
About those gloves, too...

16:35.760 --> 16:38.390
Why are you talking about those gloves all of a sudden?

16:39.350 --> 16:43.020
I reminded you of your father.

16:44.060 --> 16:47.650
What did you hear about my dad?

16:48.940 --> 16:52.030
He had small hands...

16:52.030 --> 16:54.780
and his gloves were his memento.

16:56.200 --> 16:57.370
Is that so?

16:58.070 --> 17:00.830
I'm not sure if you're understanding or not.

17:01.910 --> 17:04.290
Forget about those gloves.

17:04.290 --> 17:07.420
Those aren't worth much anyway.

17:07.420 --> 17:08.460
They must be!

17:08.460 --> 17:10.340
Because...

17:10.340 --> 17:16.340
I've seen you smiling at those gloves.

17:17.640 --> 17:19.720
You're quite observant.

17:27.940 --> 17:31.480
I hated Dad.

17:33.320 --> 17:35.030
It's true.

17:35.030 --> 17:37.200
He was serious and obstinate,

17:37.660 --> 17:41.410
and seemed to dislike whatever his son did.

17:42.330 --> 17:46.250
I was basically an enemy to him.

17:48.330 --> 17:52.050
He died in an accident at work.

17:54.550 --> 17:58.340
I couldn't help my Dad.

18:10.980 --> 18:16.650
I realized after he was gone
that his gloves were really small.

18:18.320 --> 18:20.990
It's surprisingly hard to realize,

18:20.990 --> 18:22.870
when you see it every day.

18:23.990 --> 18:28.500
I always thought he was huge and scary,

18:28.500 --> 18:33.710
but he may have been smaller than I am now.

18:34.300 --> 18:37.510
Since then, whenever I see those small gloves,

18:37.510 --> 18:39.340
I smile at them,

18:39.340 --> 18:41.260
and at myself from the past.

18:41.800 --> 18:45.020
That's why I didn't want you to touch them.

18:47.060 --> 18:50.480
I'll take you to the <i>Grand Magasin</i> someday.

18:51.440 --> 18:53.360
That's where my Dad died.

18:53.980 --> 18:57.240
That's why I was against taking you there.

18:58.860 --> 19:00.990
I see...

19:01.410 --> 19:03.330
Not yet...

19:03.330 --> 19:06.040
But when we go there,

19:06.040 --> 19:09.830
I'll tell you everything about my Dad.

19:11.420 --> 19:12.330
Okay.

19:17.130 --> 19:18.340
Look.

19:22.930 --> 19:26.220
The Galerie that my Dad loved is right here.

19:30.890 --> 19:34.190
Don't say that you can <i>only</i> do this or that.

19:34.480 --> 19:37.190
Just by seeing you safe,

19:37.190 --> 19:40.780
I feel like I'm holding onto something important.

19:45.830 --> 19:47.580
Claude-sama...

19:51.120 --> 19:52.170
Did you know?

19:52.710 --> 19:56.750
Putting a bell on a cat is an impossible task.

19:56.750 --> 19:58.000
Why?

19:58.340 --> 20:01.590
Because mice want to put the bell on the cat.

20:01.590 --> 20:03.970
They'd want to know where the cat is, right?

20:04.680 --> 20:06.010
Oh, I get it!

20:10.560 --> 20:12.640
Where are your shoes?!

20:14.480 --> 20:15.810
I'm sorry...

20:15.810 --> 20:19.070
I didn't tell you that I had to get them...

20:26.240 --> 20:27.830
Oh, Yune!

20:27.830 --> 20:29.120
Oscar-sama!

20:30.040 --> 20:32.790
What's this?

20:33.210 --> 20:35.920
She climbed up on the...

20:35.920 --> 20:38.460
Anyway, she left her shoes up there.

20:38.460 --> 20:40.840
She shouldn't be walking around without shoes, right?!

20:44.050 --> 20:47.640
I thought you would be worried, so I came...

20:50.640 --> 20:57.230
Ah, it's as if I'm in a dream

20:53.140 --> 20:54.480
Yune-chan!

20:55.230 --> 20:58.400
Oh, looks like she didn't run away, after all.

20:57.230 --> 21:03.030
As I lie here in this tender light

20:59.520 --> 21:00.530
Well, this is fine.

21:00.530 --> 21:02.900
Yune-chan!

21:02.900 --> 21:04.400
Alice-sama!

21:03.030 --> 21:14.040
When I close my eyes and listen, I can hear it

21:05.110 --> 21:07.530
I'm glad you're safe!

21:07.530 --> 21:09.660
What happened?

21:09.660 --> 21:11.700
I was so worried about you!

21:15.870 --> 21:28.930
That kind voice that warmly calls to me

21:16.250 --> 21:20.590
I'm sorry for making you all worry so much.

21:20.590 --> 21:22.130
Worry?

21:22.130 --> 21:23.260
Not at all.

21:25.260 --> 21:30.310
We're all relieved just by you being here.

21:31.510 --> 21:38.100
I want to extend my feelings with these hands

21:38.100 --> 21:44.400
We connect through our hearts, not our words

21:44.400 --> 21:51.080
Let's begin here. Let's nurture the warmth

21:50.830 --> 21:56.080
Am I part of the <i>Galerie</i> family?

21:51.080 --> 21:57.540
A new day is waiting for me

21:57.540 --> 22:09.680
I'm sure there is something here for me to protect

21:58.170 --> 21:59.290
Yeah.

22:19.650 --> 22:25.690
I want to deliver these feelings from my hands

22:26.190 --> 22:32.370
We'll be connected not only by words, but by our hearts

22:32.370 --> 22:38.620
I want to protect that dream that you created

22:38.960 --> 22:45.130
I'll be at your side, so don't lose sight of me

22:45.130 --> 22:49.840
Let's begin it here

22:51.890 --> 22:56.470
Whichever way our hearts take us

22:57.980 --> 23:02.980
Deliver them from these hands

23:04.650 --> 23:10.950
The happiness that will someday become

23:11.200 --> 23:22.290
Somebody's smile will always be here

23:24.380 --> 23:31.720
It will always stay here

23:36.810 --> 30:03.660
Thanks for watching!
